  "annotations": [
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Casting a second copy of the legendary creature Momo, Friendly Flier when one is already on the battlefield. Due to the legend rule, one copy must be sacrificed immediately, meaning the card is wasted for no board advantage. The player essentially discarded a card for nothing meaningful (just a brief +1/+1 trigger on the surviving Momo).",
      "action_taken": "Cast a second Momo, Friendly Flier while the first was already on the battlefield, triggering the legend rule and losing one copy.",
      "better_line": "Hold the second Momo as a backup for if the first dies. Instead, pass the turn or use Burst Lightning on the Tiger-Seal (a 3/3 vigilance creature that could block effectively) — though Burst Lightning only deals 2, it wouldn't kill it. Better to simply hold mana open and pass, keeping Get Lost available for a future threat and saving the redundant Momo.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 17,
      "player": "Sonnet Timmy",
      "decision_index": 8,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Missed the line of casting Sarkhan first (beholding Magmatic Hellkite from hand to create a Treasure), then using the extra Treasure to still cast Magmatic Hellkite. This would have put both a 4/5 flying Hellkite AND a 3/3 flying Sarkhan (with +1/+1 counter from Dragon entering) on the battlefield instead of just the Hellkite alone.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Magmatic Hellkite directly, using all available mana on just the one creature.",
      "better_line": "Cast Sarkhan, Dragon Ascendant first for {1}{R}, behold Magmatic Hellkite from hand to create a Treasure token, then cast Magmatic Hellkite for {2}{R}{R} using remaining 2 lands + 2 Treasures. This deploys two threats instead of one and Sarkhan grows from the Dragon entering.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 76,
      "player": "Sonnet Timmy",
      "decision_index": 16,
    }
  ],
